  ('situational-judgment-1-what-would-you-do-if-your-friend-cheated-in-an-examination', 'situational-judgment', 'Situational and Judgment Questions', 'What would you do if your friend cheated in an examination?', 'This prompt helps you practise discussing situational and judgment questions clearly and honestly. It is an educational exercise, not an official ISSB scoring criterion.', 'challenging', 'Clarify immediate risks, act fairly within your authority, communicate, and review consequences. For this question, what would you do if your friend cheated in an examination?', 'situational-practice', 'Giving extreme answers, ignoring safety or fairness, or acting beyond your authority.', 'I would punish everyone immediately without checking what happened.', 'This answer is vague, absolute, or unsupported. It gives the interviewer little reliable information about the candidate’s real behaviour.', 'I would first [practical immediate step], then [appropriate communication or escalation]. I would consider [relevant consequence] and take responsibility for my part.', '["Can you give me a specific example related to “What would you do if your friend cheated in an examination”?","What was difficult about that situation, and what did you learn?"]'::jsonb, 901),
